    {
      "id": "showroom-keep-your-work-detail",
      "type": "face",
      "label": "Keep · Reading Page",
      "position": {
        "x": -100,
        "y": -610
      },
      "width": 730,
      "height": 480,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "showroom-keep-your-work",
          "nodeId": "showroom-keep-your-work-detail"
        },
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail",
          "scroll": "page"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style=\"container-type:inline-size;box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;overflow:auto;background:#fffdf9;color:#16263d;font-family:Georgia,serif\"><div style=\"padding:clamp(24px,6cqw,65px);max-width:960px;margin:auto\"><p style=\"font:900 12px system-ui;letter-spacing:.2em;color:#8053b0\">TWILITE / KEEP THE WORK / DEMO</p><h1 style=\"font:500 clamp(45px,8cqw,78px)/1.04 Georgia,serif;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:22px 0\">The plan is still here.</h1><p style=\"font:400 clamp(20px,3cqw,27px)/1.45 Georgia,serif;color:#42546c;max-width:38ch\">An AI helped make this plan. The conversation ended. The work didn't.</p><div style=\"padding:22px 26px;background:#efeafb;border-left:5px solid #7150a4;font:600 15px/1.55 system-ui;margin:30px 0\">A fictional example, built from real editable Twilite nodes and relationships. This isn't a simulated AI session or a claim that anyone actually resumed it.</div><h2 style=\"font:500 34px Georgia,serif\">Yesterday: the conversation</h2><p style=\"font:400 18px/1.65 Georgia,serif\">“Help me organize a neighborhood movie night. We need a venue, a projector, and a way to invite people.”</p><p style=\"font:400 18px/1.65 Georgia,serif\">The agent creates a goal, tasks, and an open question. Instead of leaving the result in a chat transcript, those pieces are written into the graph document.</p><h2 style=\"font:500 34px Georgia,serif;margin-top:35px\">Today: the saved work</h2><p style=\"font:400 18px/1.65 Georgia,serif\">Inside this graph you'll find classed, editable nodes for the project and its work. The relationships are stored as edges. You can inspect the plan without reopening yesterday's conversation.</p><div style=\"border:1px solid #d2c9e6;border-radius:14px;padding:22px;background:#faf8ff\"><div style=\"font:900 12px system-ui;color:#6f4ca3;letter-spacing:.13em\">SAVED PROJECT</div><h3 style=\"font:500 28px Georgia,serif;margin:10px 0\">Neighborhood movie night</h3><p style=\"font:600 14px system-ui;margin:8px 0;color:#334155\">TASK: Confirm a location · TASK: Borrow a projector</p><p style=\"font:600 14px system-ui;margin:8px 0;color:#a66b17\">OPEN QUESTION: What if it rains?</p></div><h2 style=\"font:500 34px Georgia,serif;margin-top:35px\">Tomorrow: continue from here</h2><p style=\"font:400 18px/1.65 Georgia,serif\">Give another compatible AI access to this graph and ask: <i>“Review this project, tell me what's unresolved, and propose the next action. Ask before editing.”</i> The graph is the handoff. A real agent must read it; this example does not execute one automatically.</p><h2 style=\"font:500 34px Georgia,serif;margin-top:35px\">Your turn</h2><p style=\"font:400 18px/1.65 Georgia,serif\">Pick something you are actually planning. Ask your AI to structure it, save the graph, then reopen it in a later session. Is the work still there, still connected, and ready to continue?</p><p style=\"font:700 15px system-ui;color:#5b358f;margin:25px 0\">Create with your AI. Keep your work. Continue building.</p></div></div>"
        }
      }
    },
